# Zig Pitfalls (0.16+)

Sourced from [ziglang/zig](https://codeberg.org/ziglang/zig) issues/PRs and 0.16 release notes. Load skill **`zig-port`** when porting Modulus firmware layers.

## MUST (0.16)

- Host `main`: `pub fn main(init: std.process.Init) !void` — thread `init.gpa` and `init.io`.
- `ArrayList`: `.empty` + `ensureTotalCapacity`; `append(allocator, x)`; `deinit(allocator)`.
- Prefer **`addTranslateC`** in `build.zig` over `@cImport` (deprecated); one translate module per binary.
- `build.zig.zon`: `minimum_zig_version = "0.16.0"`; refresh deps with `zig fetch --save` — never hand-edit fingerprints.
- Tests: `std.testing.allocator` + `std.testing.io` (host only). `LeakGuard` / `withNoLeaks` for multi-phase tests (`src/modulus/testing/leak_guard.zig`).
- Leak check: `std.heap.DebugAllocator` (0.16); not `GeneralPurposeAllocator`.
- Firmware translate-C: **same** `-target` as link (`riscv32-freestanding-none` for P4 objects).
- Pin Zig patch version in CI; re-run full test after compiler bump.

## NEVER

- `std.io` (lowercase), `ArrayList.init`, `list.writer()`, `list.append(x)` without allocator — pre-0.16 APIs.
- `@Type(...)` — use `@Struct`, `@Int`, `@Tuple`, `@Pointer`, etc.
- `Io.Threaded.init_single_threaded` deep in libraries (smell: use injected `io` from `main`).
- Circular `build.zig` module imports (0.16 DAG rejects loops).
- `packed struct` as function return @ ReleaseSafe ([#35634](https://codeberg.org/ziglang/zig/issues/35634)).
- Odd-width ints (`i24`) in protocol code on self-hosted backend ([#35597](https://codeberg.org/ziglang/zig/issues/35597)).
- `bool` across C FFI without ABI verification ([#35373](https://codeberg.org/ziglang/zig/issues/35373)) — prefer `c_int` in new shims.
- Heap alloc in Core 1 / ISR / 1 kHz+ loops (Modulus hot path).
- Incremental `--watch` inside `/tmp` ([#35365](https://codeberg.org/ziglang/zig/issues/35365)) — stale binaries.
- Port C6 ESP-Hosted slave to Zig (stay C 1.4.0).

## When build breaks

1. `zig build -fno-incremental` then clean `zig-out` / project `zig-pkg/`.
2. Check optimize mode (ReleaseSmall miscompiles: [#35560](https://codeberg.org/ziglang/zig/issues/35560)).
3. Search [Codeberg issues](https://codeberg.org/ziglang/zig/issues) (new ≥30000); GitHub read-only for history.
4. Minimal repro before blaming application code.

## Upstream

- Canonical repo: **Codeberg** (not GitHub for new issues).
- Zig 0.16.x: *"This Release Contains Bugs"* — non-trivial projects may need pinned compiler or master tracking.
